  "answer": "Before promising enterprise deployment dates, sales should use the **\"Corpus Readiness Checklist\"** during the discovery phase [NL-015#NL-015-S04][NL-023#NL-023-S07]. This checklist must require Enterprise prospects to submit a **sample of 20 core documents for format analysis** [NL-031#NL-031-S06]. Its primary focus is identifying **scanned, image-only PDFs** that lack a text layer and require OCR [NL-015#NL-015-S04][NL-031#NL-031-S06]. If such scanned PDFs are detected, sales must flag them early so the Customer Success team can adjust the target timeline — otherwise, the standard Enterprise onboarding expectation of 8–10 weeks (actual median 8.7 weeks) may be missed, and the pilot would fail the 85% citation correctness go-live threshold [NL-015#NL-015-S04][NL-031#NL-031-S02]. This checklist manages customer expectations around delayed onboarding unless they run OCR on their end first [NL-015#NL-015-S04].\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
